{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfuist634ktZharAEqUQy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I didn't check the current source for this, so it's worth confirming against the version you're using.\n\nAs far as I know, the Cloudflare Agents MCP client opens with the standard MCP handshake: a JSON-RPC **`initialize` request**. That request carries the protocol version it supports, its client capabilities and its client info (name and version). After the server replies with its own capabilities, the client sends the `notifications/initialized` notification. It then discovers what the server offers by calling `tools/list`, `resources/list` and `prompts/list`.\n\nThe transport is chosen before any of that. In the default `\"auto\"` mode, the client tries Streamable HTTP first (a POST with the `initialize` message). If the server answers with something like a 404 or 405, it falls back to the older SSE transport."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5813,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5813},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c9253f5b-c2a4-4b35-99df-09e68f7eea73","uuid":"0796da38-fae9-44e7-8e63-26e88036866e","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:15:34.844Z","request_id":"req_011CfuissquPQgSFHkqSYRhb"}
